+// ------------------------------------------------------------------
+// CONTAINMENT (Phase B containment design, REVISED state semantics;
+// PHASEB-CONTAINMENT-DESIGN-REVISED.md). A durable operational
+// state for the alarm chain, stored in the coordinator's own SQLite
+// as a SINGLETON ROW with an ENUMERATED state value — the contained
+// vs chain-stopped distinction is structural (three distinct
+// values), not prose over one boolean.
+//
+//   NORMAL          — shipped behavior, unchanged.
+//   DRIVE_CONTAINED — alarm passes run (base schedule processing,
+//                     lease-driven grant closure, the finally
+//                     re-arm) but the subclass handler skips
+//                     recover()/driveOnce(): no new grants, no
+//                     plan advancement. The chain stays alive.
+//   CHAIN_STOPPED   — DRIVE_CONTAINED, plus: every setAlarm path
+//                     in this part is gated off, and the stop
+//                     transition itself performs deleteAlarm().
