+// Read discipline (the fail-closed core):
+//   * Reads NEVER write and NEVER create the tables. The tables
+//     are created ONLY by a transition (applyContainmentTransition
+//     below), so an ABSENT table is a structurally verified NORMAL:
+//     no transition has ever been recorded, hence no stop exists
+//     that a read failure could defeat.
+//   * Any OTHER read failure (or an unrecognized stored value)
+//     yields verified=false, and every consuming path defaults
+//     DARKER: drive is treated as contained, arming is treated as
+//     stopped. A read failure can therefore never silently defeat
+//     a recorded stop: with the table present and a stop recorded,
+//     a failed read suppresses registration instead of permitting
+//     it, and the suppression is itself recorded (transitions
+//     ledger, best-effort; the recorder's armed_after on the next
+//     pass is the second witness).
+//   * A stop is VERIFIED only by evidence after the act: the
+//     transition reads the state row back AND reads getAlarm()
+//     (must be null). An unverified stop is reported as such —
+//     outcome "rejected", reason containment_stop_unverified —
+//     with the state row left at CHAIN_STOPPED (darker), never as
+//     a silent success.
+//
+// V3 ADDENDUM (Phase B containment design v3;
+// PHASEB-CONTAINMENT-DESIGN-V3.md; Rowan containment-correction
